import scene_queries.dl
import camera.dl

to get [the website Farm view from] {vector:eye} [toward] {vector:target} [is blocked by] {UI scene objects:objects}:
    for each height in [-0.15,0.35]:
        set subject to target + (a UI scene vector from [0.0,height,0.0])
        set distance to the length of (subject - eye)
        set ray to @intrinsic("construct", UI scene ray, the UI scene vector form of eye, (subject - eye) normalized)
        set selected to the UI scene object selection from ray among objects including backfaces false
        if (selected's selection's hit's hit) and (selected's selection's hit's distance < distance - 0.1):
            return true
    return false

to [focus website Farm camera] {a pointer to website Farm camera:camera} [on] {a pointer to website farm actor:actor} [in] {a pointer to website farm world:world} [around] {a pointer to website Farm landscape:landscape} [over] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    set target to (the website Farm scene point at (actor's x) (actor's y) in world) + (a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.45,0.0])
    set objects to the website Farm occluders in landscape
    set eye to target
    set index to 0
    set blocked to true
    loop while (index < 12) and blocked:
        set angle to (the website Farm heading for (actor's direction)) + index * 0.5235987755982988
        set direction to a UI scene vector from [(the sine of angle),0.9,(the cosine of angle)]
        set eye to target + (direction normalized) * 7.0
        set blocked to the website Farm view from eye toward target is blocked by objects
        increment index
    free objects
    focus website Farm camera camera on target viewed from eye over seconds seconds
